 "lineas": [
  {
   "texto": "You need a house, so you build it right on top of the ground. Problem solved!",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "But the topsoil is soft, and the heavy walls slowly sink into it.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "And they sink unevenly, so the walls crack.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "So you pour wide concrete feet under every wall. Footings spread the weight out.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "But dig deeper, and under the topsoil there's thick, soft clay that still squeezes down.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "So you drive concrete piles all the way down, until they stand on solid rock.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "A concrete beam ties the tops together, so every wall moves as one.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "But water creeps up through the concrete and rots the bottom of the walls.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "So you wrap the beam in a waterproof layer before the walls go up.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "Congratulations! You just built a house foundation. What should we build next?",
   "pausa": 0.2
  }
 ],
